---
// About section: bio + photo placeholder
---

<section id="hello" class="py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-12 md:gap-16 items-start">

      <!-- Photo placeholder -->
      <div class="md:col-span-1 flex justify-center md:justify-start">
        <div
          class="w-48 h-48 md:w-full md:h-auto md:aspect-square rounded-2xl bg-[#8b6f47]/10 dark:bg-[#8b6f47]/15 flex items-center justify-center"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <span class="font-serif text-6xl font-bold text-[#8b6f47]/40 select-none">
            J
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Bio -->
      <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-[#1a1916] dark:text-[#e8e6e1] mb-6">
          Hello.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-[#6b6760] dark:text-[#9b9790] leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            I've been writing code since 2011 — long enough to have strong opinions,
            short enough to still find it genuinely exciting. Since then I've built
            full-stack web applications for startups and large organisations, earned an
            MSc in Mathematics, and eventually went freelance, which is a polite way of
            saying I opted out of the open-plan office.
          </p>
          <p>
            These days I work as a freelance engineer and consultant, mostly in JavaScript
            and TypeScript. I like early-stage work: the messy, exciting bit where things
            are still taking shape.
          </p>
          <p>
            I'm active in Berlin's tech community: organising meetups for freelancers,
            speaking at events, and the occasional podcast appearance. The thread running
            through all of it is the human side of tech — careers, community, and finding
            a way of working that actually fits your life.
          </p>
          <p class="italic">
            I read, I speak, I write, I code.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
